\section{Numerical Architecture}
\subsection{Relativistic MHD Equations}
The RMHD system evolves the conserved variables:
\[
\mathbf{U} = 
\begin{pmatrix}
D \\ \bm{S} \\ \tau \\ \bm{B}
\end{pmatrix},
\]
where $D$ is the generalized density, $\bm{S}$ momentum density, $\tau$ total energy, and $\bm{B}$ magnetic field.

The fluxes are computed using an exact HLLC Riemann solver:
\[
\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{U}) = 
\begin{pmatrix}
D v_i \\
S_j v_i + P^\ast \delta_{ij} - B_j B_i \\
(\tau + P^\ast) v_i - (\bm{B}\cdot\bm{v}) B_i \\
v_i B_j - v_j B_i
\end{pmatrix}.
\]

\subsection{Constrained Transport}
Magnetic divergence is controlled via CT:
\[
\nabla \cdot \bm{B} = 0 + \mathcal{O}(10^{-16}),
\]
ensuring machine-precision stability.

\subsection{Symplectic Integration}
The Hamiltonian is preserved through a second-order symplectic scheme:
\[
H = \int \left( \frac{1}{2}\rho v^2 + \epsilon + \frac{B^2}{2} \right) d^3x.
\]

